Apple plans to unveil 14-inch and 16-inch MacBook Pro models with touch-enabled OLED displays on Wednesday, October 28, according to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman. Those invited to Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/19/apple-pro-and-tell/">"Pro and tell" experience</a> in Los Angeles at 10 a.m. Pacific Time on that day will likely receive hands-on time with the laptops after they are announced in a press release.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/MacBook-Pro-Dynamic-Island-multicolor.jpg" alt="" width="2100" height="1181" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1071828" /><br/>
In his <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-10-25/apple-to-unveil-touch-screen-macbook-pro-executive-promotions-in-box-checker"><em>Power On</em> newsletter today</a>, Gurman reiterated that these MacBook Pro models will look similar to the current models, but weigh less and feature a Dynamic Island instead of a notch at the top of the screen. He previously reported that the laptops will be powered by Apple's existing M5 Pro and M5 Max chips released back in March.<br/>
<br/>
With a costlier OLED display, the new MacBook Pro models are expected to be more expensive. In the U.S., pricing for the existing models with mini-LED displays and M5 Pro and M5 Max chips starts at &#36;2,499 for the 14-inch model and at &#36;2,999 for the 16-inch model, and starting prices for the new models could be up to &#36;500 higher.<br/>
<br/>
macOS Golden Gate is said to feature a "dynamic interface" for touch input.<br/>
<br/>
"The system will take previous interactions into account, presenting controls based on whether someone has been touching the display or using the trackpad," explained Gurman. "Touching a button can also bring up a menu around the user's finger, while the Dock and Menu Bar have been optimized for touch."<br/>
<br/>
Apple will position touch as an additional input method that customers can use when it makes sense, alongside the keyboard and trackpad, he said.<br/>
<br/>
